        "thinking": "I'm checking the root पॄ, meaning \"to fill/protect,\" in the juhotyādi class, noting that its short-ṛ anudātta marking would indicate it's aniṭ, and comparing this against different versions of the Dhatupatha.\n\nSince 7.2.70 inserts iṭ before sya in lṛṭ/lṛṅ regardless, I work out that the second person plural lṛṅ parasmaipada form is अपरिष्यत, with guṇa turning पृ into पर् before adding इष्य; if the root were actually long पॄ, vikalpa would also allow अपरीष्यत, but अपरिष्यत is valid either way.\n\n",
